          <!-- 02 · The model journey: data → input features → interpretability → final model -->
          <section class="cs-section" id="bb-model">
            <header class="cs-section-head">
              <span class="cs-num">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Building the punch-recognition model</h3>
                <p class="cs-lead">The challenge: teach a small onboard computer to tell jabs, hooks, uppercuts and
                  blocks apart <mark>in a split second</mark>, while gloves hide the hands.</p>
              </div>
            </header>

            <div class="cs-journey">
            <div class="cs-step" id="bb-model-data">
              <h4>Record punches, then label every one</h4>
              <p class="cs-takeaway">I recorded boxers with a depth camera and built my own tool to label every
                punch.</p>
              <p>An early test exposed the big problem straight away: <mark>boxing gloves hide the wrists</mark>, so
                normal skeleton tracking loses the hands.</p>
              <div class="cs-media-lg">
                <figure style="--ar: 1.792"><img class="js-lightbox"
                    src="assets/boxbunny_capstone/annotation_gui.webp" alt="RGB-D annotation GUI" loading="lazy">
                  <figcaption>My labelling tool for colour + depth clips</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure style="--ar: 1.741"><img class="js-lightbox"
                    src="assets/boxbunny_capstone/3d_pose_estimation.webp" alt="3D pose estimation" loading="lazy">
                  <figcaption>Skeleton tracking losing the gloved hands</figcaption>
                </figure>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cs-step" id="bb-model-tries">
              <h4>Exploring input features</h4>
              <p class="cs-takeaway">Every approach failed in a different way, and each failure pointed to the next
                idea.</p>

              <div class="cs-sub">
                <p class="cs-sub-label">First, eight ways to "see" a punch</p>
                <p>The same clip, shown eight ways. Each panel is a different kind of input the model could learn
                  from: skeletons, 3D blocks (voxels), cropped images, outlines and glove tracking.</p>
              </div>
              <figure class="feature-compare-video">
                <video controls autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/boxbunny_capstone/feature_comparison_poster.webp">
                  <source src="assets/boxbunny_capstone/feature_comparison.mp4" type="video/mp4">
                </video>
                <figcaption>Eight input types running on the same clip</figcaption>
              </figure>

              <div class="cs-sub">
                <p class="cs-sub-label">How the nine iterations played out</p>
                <p>Pose, pixels and voxels each failed on their own. <mark>Fusing voxels with pose</mark> fixed both
                  weaknesses.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="phases-diagram">
                <div class="phases-grid">
                  <div class="phase-col phase-pose">
                    <div class="phase-head">Pose (iter 1–2)</div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>1. 2D Pose + LSTM</strong>
                      <span class="fail">✗ Wrong camera angle</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>2. 3D Pose</strong> (depth lifting, ~67%)
                      <span class="fail">✗ Glove occlusion blocks wrists</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-lesson">
                      <strong>Lesson:</strong> skeleton joints carry hand identity, but pose alone is not reliable
                      under occlusion.
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-note">Pose returns later ↓</div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="phase-col phase-pixels">
                    <div class="phase-head">Raw Pixels (iter 3–4)</div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>3. Raw RGBD + 3D CNN</strong> (87.2%)
                      <span class="fail">✗ 88M params, too large for Jetson</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>4. RGBD + Segmentation</strong>
                      <span class="fail">✗ Still pixel-based, still required Colab</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-lesson">
                      <strong>Lesson:</strong> need compact, engineered features; raw pixels are too heavy for edge
                      deployment.
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-note">Dead end, redirected the search</div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="phase-col phase-voxel">
                    <div class="phase-head">Voxels (iter 5–7)</div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>5. Z-Mask</strong> (2D depth grid)
                      <span class="fail">✗ Lost 3D spatial information</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>6. Voxel + Colour</strong> (~96%)
                      <span class="fail">✗ Impractical coloured gloves</span>
                      <span class="insight">★ Insight: voxels need hand info</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-step">
                      <strong>7. Voxel-Only</strong> (80.6%)
                      <span class="fail">✗ Left/right confusion (34% jab error)</span>
                      <span class="insight">★ Insight: need pose back for L/R</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="phase-arrow">↓</div>
                    <div class="phase-lesson">
                      <strong>Lesson:</strong> 3D motion is the right primary signal, but voxels alone cannot
                      distinguish left from right hand.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="phase-merge" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 960 80" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <line x1="160" y1="0" x2="160" y2="30" stroke="#1565c0" stroke-width="2"/>
