                <figcaption>Final prototype</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure style="--ar: 0.809">
                <img class="js-lightbox" src="assets/robotic_companion/final_side.png"
                  alt="Robotic Companion head design in SolidWorks, side view" loading="lazy">
                <figcaption>Head design in SolidWorks</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 01 · What the user experiences -->
          <section class="cs-section" id="rc-reacts">
            <header class="cs-section-head">
              <span class="cs-num">01</span>
              <div>
                <h3>It doesn't just listen · it reacts</h3>
                <p class="cs-lead">The robot's mood is a <mark>direct response to yours</mark>.</p>
              </div>
            </header>
            <div class="cs-parts rc-loop">
              <div>
                <h5>Sees you</h5>
                <p>The camera finds your face and keeps it in view.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h5>Reads your mood</h5>
                <p>It measures <mark>how positive and how energetic</mark> you look, and passes that to the AI.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h5>Shows how it feels</h5>
                <p>Every reply carries a mood tag that picks one of <mark>13 animated faces</mark> on its screen.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="media-layout media-layout-2 cs-face-pair">
              <figure>
                <img class="js-lightbox" src="assets/robotic_companion/robot_neutral_face.jpg"
                  alt="ESP32 touchscreen face with neutral expression" loading="lazy">
                <figcaption>Neutral face · one of 13 expressions</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/gui_emotion_circumplex.png"
                  alt="Emotion circumplex plot with live valence/arousal data" loading="lazy">
                <figcaption>Live mood readout · positive → right, energetic → up</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 02 · Software: voice loop + face in parallel -->
          <section class="cs-section" id="rc-turn">
            <header class="cs-section-head">
              <span class="cs-num">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3>What happens in one conversation turn</h3>
                <p class="cs-lead">You stop talking, and it starts replying <mark>in under 0.8 seconds</mark>, all on
                  the robot.</p>
              </div>
            </header>
            <div class="rc-turn-grid">
              <div class="rc-turn-col">
                <p class="cs-sub-label">The voice loop</p>
                <ol class="cs-flow">
                  <li><b>Hears you finish</b> and cuts out the clip of your speech.</li>
                  <li><b>Writes down</b> what you said, as you say it.</li>
                  <li><b>Thinks of a reply</b>, with your mood and the chat so far in the prompt.</li>
                  <li><b>Speaks it</b> sentence by sentence, so it <mark>starts talking before the full reply is
                      ready</mark>.</li>
                </ol>
              </div>
              <div class="rc-turn-col rc-turn-side">
                <p class="cs-sub-label">Meanwhile, the face</p>
                <ul class="cs-list">
                  <li><b>Expression</b> switches to match the reply's mood tag.</li>
                  <li><b>Lips move</b> in time with the voice, about 30 times a second.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="cs-note">It runs on a separate branch, so the face <mark>never holds up the voice</mark>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figure class="arch-figure">
              <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/turn_sequence.svg"
                alt="Conversation turn sequence · voice pipeline from microphone to TTS, with face branch for affect and visemes"
                loading="lazy">
              <figcaption>One turn · voice runs left to right, the face branch drops down in parallel</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="media-layout media-layout-2 rc-pipes">
              <figure>
                <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/audio_pipeline.svg"
                  alt="Audio pipeline · mic array to speech output" loading="lazy">
                <figcaption>Audio pipeline · mic to speaker</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <figure>
                <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/vision_pipeline.svg"
                  alt="Vision pipeline · face detection to emotion classification" loading="lazy">
                <figcaption>Vision pipeline · camera to mood</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 03 · Hardware: mechanism + wiring -->
          <section class="cs-section" id="rc-hardware">
            <header class="cs-section-head">
              <span class="cs-num">03</span>
              <div>
                <h3>The hardware · designed and built solo</h3>
                <p class="cs-lead">A custom head that can <mark>nod and turn</mark>, and one computer wired to every
                  part.</p>
              </div>
            </header>

            <div class="cs-step" id="rc-hardware-mech">
              <h4><span class="cs-step-tag">Mechanism</span> Two motors, one gear, a head that nods and turns</h4>
              <p class="cs-takeaway">Both motors drive a shared gear, so together they control both directions of
                movement.</p>
              <div class="cs-parts rc-motion">
                <div>
                  <h5>Nod (tilt)</h5>
                  <p>Both motors turn <mark>the same way</mark>.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h5>Turn (pan)</h5>
                  <p>The motors turn <mark>opposite ways</mark>.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="cs-mech-row">
                <figure class="companion-video">
                  <video controls autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="none" poster="assets/robotic_companion/live_motor_control_with_kinematics_poster.webp">
                    <source src="assets/robotic_companion/live_motor_control_with_kinematics.mp4" type="video/mp4">
                  </video>
                  <figcaption>I move the 3D head on screen · the real head follows live</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain"
                    src="assets/robotic_companion/differential_bevel.svg"
                    alt="Differential bevel-gear head mechanism" loading="lazy">
                  <figcaption>The gear layout + the maths behind it</figcaption>
                </figure>
              </div>
              <div class="cs-sub">
                <p class="cs-sub-label">Six versions to get it smooth</p>
                <p>Designed in SolidWorks. Each version fixed a problem: <mark>cable routing, pivot alignment and
                    3D-print warping</mark>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="cs-media-3 rc-evolution">
                <figure>
                  <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/prototype_1.png"
                    alt="Head design, version 1" loading="lazy">
                  <figcaption>Version 1</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/prototype_5.png"
                    alt="Head design, version 5" loading="lazy">
                  <figcaption>Version 5</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                  <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/final_front.png"
                    alt="Final head mechanism, front view" loading="lazy">
                  <figcaption>Final</figcaption>
                </figure>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cs-step" id="rc-hardware-wiring">
              <h4><span class="cs-step-tag">Wiring</span> The full robot at a glance</h4>
              <p class="cs-takeaway">One Jetson Orin Nano in the middle. The camera, mic, face screen, speaker and
                both motors each plug straight into it.</p>
              <p>Every line below is a <mark>real cable on the robot today</mark>. Both motors share a single bus
                adapter (CH343).</p>
              <figure class="arch-figure">
                <img class="js-lightbox media-fit-contain" src="assets/robotic_companion/hardware_topology.svg"
                  alt="Hardware topology · Jetson Orin Nano hub connected to camera, mic, ESP32 face, speaker, bus adapter and two servos"
                  loading="lazy">
                <figcaption>Hardware map · every part is a direct link to the Jetson</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>

            <p class="callout-strip"><span class="callout-chip">6 hardware iterations</span><span
                class="callout-chip">Config-swappable LLM/STT/TTS</span><span class="callout-chip">Watchdog + graceful
                degradation</span><span class="callout-chip">Jetson + ESP32 multi-MCU</span></p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>
